Note review_status {
  '''
    DRAFT 1 — visual review before the first migration.
    Apply v0.7 with entity map v0.8 and the dated October 22/23 review decisions.
    Sale status is mutually exclusive; opening Purchase dates use the approved second-day convention.
    Money is integer centavos; occurrence timestamps are timestamptz.
    This review is not executable migration evidence.
    All explicit secondary indexes are standalone Organization lookups.
    Primary keys remain; BusinessEvent/detail indexes are still deferred.
    Required scoped keys, readable-ID/collection uniqueness and concurrency enforcement
    remain T01 obligations; conceptual composite references are not executable FKs yet.
    All candidate table shapes are rejected and absent; remaining storage work is in design.md.
  '''
}

Note embedded_and_derived_entries {
  '''
    Mapped without separate tables:
    E15 expense payment information -> purchase_expense_payments / sale_expense_payments,
        with reconciled settled_amount totals and completion timestamps on expenses.
    E33 ItemHistoryEntry -> timeline over Item-linked sources and shared history.
    E34 FinancialEffect -> reporting projection over dated source facts/adjustments.
    E35 AuditEntry -> BusinessEvent plus typed change details.
    E42 Product image values -> products.images (text array; hosting still open).
    E39 OpeningAcquisition -> marked purchases grouped by Supplier and year/month,
        conventionally dated the second day at 00:00 UTC.
    E40/E41 import operation/row evidence -> T05 artifacts, no persistent tables.
    E36/E37 -> approved dedicated customer/supplier settlement headers and source portions.
        Rejected generic mixed-party settlement boxes are absent.
    E43 Brand value -> products.brand.
    E44 ItemCostSnapshot -> InventoryItem snapshot fields plus preserved allocations;
        a separate versioned record remains conditional on D06.
    No Reservation, Garage, Collection, credit, balance, Profit or LossRecovery table.
    Retired E12, E17, E22, E23, E30, E31 and E38 are not reused.
  '''
}

Note shared_expense_example {
  '''
    P1 has I1/I2; P2 has I3/I4, all in the same Organization.
    One BRL 30 PurchaseExpense links P1 and P2.
    Allocate BRL 10 to I1 and BRL 20 to I4; I2/I3 receive none.
    Purchase subtotals derive as 10/20; source cost stays 30 once.
    Paying 10 then 20 records two dated cash payments; settled_amount progresses 0/10/30.
    Completing P1 preserves P2's independent progress and every protected unit cost.
  '''
}

Note policy_boundaries {
  '''
    D01 partial-Return funding-source selection; D02 historical collection presentation;
    D03 negative recovery profit; D04 public catalog fields/context/images;
    D05 report/average-cost basis; D06 exceptional corrections and expense disposition;
    D07 existing shared Product edits/global audit/private annotations/historical labels;
    D08 finalization of never-approved collection-unit costs.
    T02 remaining access/session/bootstrap; T03 exact money/business dates;
    T05 reviewed opening acquisition and spreadsheet mapping.
    No policy is selected merely by drawing a table or relationship here.
  '''
}
